// THE REFUSING HALF of the bare-place receiver loan (borrow_check.cpp,
// MethodCall). Paired with tests/logos/pass/bc_recvresv_two_phase_legal.logos,
// which pins the two-phase shapes that must stay legal.
//
// A `&self` method whose ARGUMENT calls a `&mut self` method on the same
// receiver. rustc E0502. `self` is a reference param, so sema never wraps it in
// an AddrOfTemp — this receiver spelling had NO producer at all: the conflict
// was checked and the loan was never recorded, so nothing held `self` while the
// arguments were evaluated. That it was admitted at HEAD is not an assertion
// here, it is the deleted ledger row: this is the native twin of
// tests/imported/fail/borrowck/suggest-local-var-imm-and-mut, which sat in
// bc_admits.ledger until the deposit landed.
//
// ⚠ THE `&mut self` × `&mut self` TWIN IS *NOT* CLOSED. `self.set(self.set(1))`
// — rustc E0499 — is still admitted: traced, its receivers arrive at visit()'s
// AddrOfTemp arm instead of at check_recv_conflict, so neither the deposit here
// nor a reservation arm at that function can see them. The hole is real, it is
// named at both sites, and it is not asserted by any fixture.
package bc_recvresv_shared_recv_mut_arg_fail;

struct Foo { n: i64 }

impl Foo {
    fn foo(self: &Self, q: i64) -> i64 { return self.n + q; }
    fn bar(self: &mut Self) -> i64 { self.n = self.n + 1i64; return self.n; }
    fn baz(self: &mut Self) -> i64 { return self.foo(self.bar()); }
}

fn main() -> i32 {
    let mut f: Foo = Foo { n: 0i64 };
    return f.baz() as i32;
}
